# GluRun SDK: what this stable-diffusion.cpp tree is.
#
# This is the `glurun/main` branch of https://github.com/GluLabs-ai/stable-diffusion.cpp -
# leejet/stable-diffusion.cpp at the sha below with GluRun's commits on top, one per change.
# engines/sd/stable-diffusion.cpp in the GluRun SDK is a submodule pinned to its head.
#
# The vendored ggml gets the same treatment, but without a second repository: .gitmodules here
# points `ggml` back at this repository, branch `glurun/ggml` (leejet/ggml with our four
# commits and a .glurun-base of its own). `git submodule update --init --recursive` therefore
# gets both trees from one clone, and each side can still follow its own upstream with an
# ordinary merge. The two histories in this repository are unrelated, exactly as
# leejet/stable-diffusion.cpp and leejet/ggml are.
#
# engines/sd/CMakeLists.txt reads this file and the one in ggml/ at configure time and refuses
# to build if either is missing or lacks a feature the SDK needs, with a message telling you to
# run `git submodule update --init --recursive`. Nothing is patched at build time
# (docs/BUILD.md "The image engine's base").
#
# Adding a change: commit it on this branch, add a feature= line here in the same commit, push,
# then bump the submodule in the SDK and add the id to GLURUN_SD_BASE_FEATURES in
# engines/sd/CMakeLists.txt if the SDK depends on it.
branch=glurun/main
fork=https://github.com/GluLabs-ai/stable-diffusion.cpp
upstream=c678dfe704a2230342376b46add9c8ca736a653d
upstream_url=https://github.com/leejet/stable-diffusion.cpp
ggml_branch=glurun/ggml
feature=gpu-placement-and-attention
feature=precomputed-conditioning
feature=lazy-disk-params
